```python
from object_detector import Object_Detector_Tool
from text_detector import Text_Detector_Tool
from letter_detector import Letter_Detector_Tool
from pixel_level_depth_estimator import Pixel_Depth_Tool

# Assuming the image file path is provided
image_path = "path/to/image.png"

# Detecting objects based on the text in the image
detected_objects = Object_Detector_Tool.execute(image=image_path)
object_number = detected_objects.object_number

# Detecting specific letters in the image
letter_results = Letter_Detector_Tool.execute(image=image_path)

# Assuming the depth result is required by other tools
depth_results = Pixel_Depth_Tool.execute(image_path=image_path)

# Assuming the depth results are required by other tools
visited_depth_images = Pixel_Depth_Tool.execute(image_path=image_path, output=True)
```

This program loads the object detector, text detector, letter detector, and pixel depth estimation tools. It assumes the image file path is provided and executes the tools accordingly. The results are stored in variables `detected_objects`, `letter_results`, and `visited_depth_images`. The `depth_results` variable contains the information about the depth of the image based on the depth estimation tool.
